Z||000000||Ronnie||05-23-2001||10:03 PM||||Does anyone have a list of the classes that will be in the show in August?||||reg||6
Z||000001||FieroHarry||05-24-2001||08:02 AM||||Okay Im not going to retype this whole thing,<P>Stock class (all years and models)<BR>Custom judged (coupes/gts)<BR>Semi-Mod Judged (coupes/gt/in progress)<BR>Full-Mod Judged (coupe/gt/unfinished)<BR>replicars (pro built/owner built)<BR>Historical (coupe/gt)<P>For more info on judging/rules find a friend with the current issue of FOCOA Fiero owners magazine. Also try the web site at <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroowners.com</A> <P>PS if you have a particular question for your class e-mail me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||08:09 AM||||What's the difference between the 'Historical' class and the 'Stock' class?<P>And how close to 100% stock does an entrant into the 'Stock' class have to be, to keep from getting booted into the 'Custom' class? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||08:10 AM||||Oh, and do all entrants have to be pre-registered, or can we sign up and pay the fees when we arrive?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHarry||05-24-2001||09:21 AM||||STOCK: In this group you will be allowed at least 5 small changes. No wheel changes, however you may upgrade within the fiero wheels....<BR>Car should still look basically stock, however you may upgrade paint, but must be stock Fiero and year appropriate..yada yada<BR>Nine classes in "stock"<BR>NOTE: You will only be judged with cars of the same grouping ie: 85 GT "Sunroof"<BR>tee tops are judged against t-tops/ sun roofs against sun roofs etc etc<P><BR>CUSTOM: You are allowed up to 10 changes. This is where you have taken a stock car and personelized it. Paint, wheel & tires. Floor mats,sidescoops and small mechanical upgrades. updates, add-ons etc<P>Yes you can pay your registration the day of the show!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||05-24-2001||09:45 AM||||Here the link<BR> <A HREF="http://www.vafieros.com/news.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.vafieros.com/news.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierodave2001||05-24-2001||09:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHarry:<BR><B>Stock class (all years and models)<BR>Custom judged (coupes/gts)<BR>Semi-Mod Judged (coupes/gt/in progress)<BR>Full-Mod Judged (coupe/gt/unfinished)<BR>replicars (pro built/owner built)<BR>Historical (coupe/gt)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>FieroHarry,<BR>Question,  the past few shows, I've entered as stock, and Carlile as "Factory Stock"<P>Now this is the first time I've seen the "Historical" class.<P>Which do you think I should enter as for Williamsburg?<P>I'm looking at the Historical class, but not sure.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroDave.jpg"> <BR>Thank you for any information.||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||09:59 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>STOCK: In this group you will be allowed at least 5 small changes. No wheel changes, however you may upgrade within the fiero wheels....<BR>Car should still look basically stock, however you may upgrade paint, but must be stock Fiero and year appropriate..yada yada<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Up to 5 small changes? Sweet! I'm golden there...<P><BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Nine classes in "stock"<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow... let's see if I can guess them all...<BR>1. '84 Coupe<BR>2. '84 Indy Replica<BR>3. '85-'86 4-cyl Coupe<BR>4. '85-'86 V6 (SE/GT)<BR>5. '87 4-cyl Coupe<BR>6. '87 V6 (SE/GT)<BR>7. '88 4-cyl Coupe<BR>8. '88 V6 GT<BR>9. '88 V6 Formula<P>No, those don't really look right... too many overlaps in the coverage... I couldn't get the fieroowners link to work... where can I find these out?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>NOTE: You will only be judged with cars of the same grouping ie: 85 GT "Sunroof"<BR>tee tops are judged against t-tops/ sun roofs against sun roofs etc etc<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I tried to take this info into consideration with my guesses above, but couldn't figure out how to make it work and only have 9 classes...<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Yes you can pay your registration the day of the show!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cool beans... is there anything we'd be missing out on (or screwing up) by waiting until we get there to just show up and say "Hi! We've got our hotel room and our Fieros, but you don't know about us yet... where do we sign up and pay?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||05-24-2001||10:01 AM||||Hi Fierodave2001, Reading the material from their page I think the historical group is for cars like yours - Absolutely perfectly stock and gorgeous ||||reg||1
Z||000009||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||10:02 AM||||FieroDave - enter whatever class you want to that I'm *not* in...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(Got a stock '88 Formula..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P><BR>EDIT - found the info - printed the forms... thanks for the link...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
