Z||000011||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||10:40 AM||||Actually, um, no, I'll... um... be in the *other* Formula class... yeah, that's it... the "Didn't-used-to-be-a-prize-winning-GT-but-now-it's-a-Formula" class...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Old Lar||05-24-2001||01:04 PM||||Historical class is as built.  A car for the purist who have a reference point as to questions on the car.  There are a few out there and the competition can be tough.<P>Stock class IMO, is for cars that have been driven.  I've seen stock cars with 100000 miles + (Michelle Ruscoe's coupe)on them that are in pristine condition.  To have them compete against a brand new low milage car in the same class puts them at a huge disadvantage.  Popular vote can have strange results.  If you ratio condition vs milage, the high milage car's position improves.<P>Daytona with "independent" judges is a way to go with cars all meeting the same judged criteria. Personal preferences vary so much.<P>There are low milage cars that show up at the national show that can be in a class all there own.  The best of the best.||||reg||3
Z||000013||Black88GT||05-24-2001||04:12 PM||||Is this one judged or popular vote?||||reg||1
Z||000014||Au nrod||05-24-2001||04:42 PM||||this is a popular vote show. good luck! i go not expecting anything, and should i luck out, then i thank my lucky star. pop vote can be rough. i was at one show and seen several guys look and vote on red cars only.<BR>let me correct myself. since i go in the pop vote all the time, i forgot a few years ago the did start judging the 'custom' class, the 'semi-mod' & the 'full-mod', along with the 'replicas' & the 'historical'.. sorry for the misinformation. must have had a senior moment<P>   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Is this one judged or popular vote?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>[This message has been edited by Au nrod (edited 05-24-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Au nrod (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroHarry||05-24-2001||06:19 PM||||Fiero"Dave"2001,<P>My best guess for you would be as replied above.<BR>Go for the historicaL class. I feel either way you go you are a shoe in and this would give others in "stock" a chance at first place.<BR>Fortunalty for you (unfortunate for others) you have a pristine "show room" ride with nothing for mileage. A serious advantage over most others!<P>If you would like a better answer please ask<BR>CaptFiero or Phil&Gloria from FOCOA.<BR>They have much more experiance than I in judging events for Fiero's and could give you a better answer than me. I would hate to tell you the wrong thing!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>My old clunker has way to many changes and has to play against the "Big Dogs" so I expect nothing unless two other people from Carlisle dont show up.<BR>Then maybe just maybe I'll get lucky and take "Highest Mileage" ( fat chance at that one)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||14
Z||000016||Fierochic88||05-24-2001||11:52 PM||||Fiero Harry or anyone else who knows.  Are the cars definitely being separated to roof type no matter what?  They did this in Columbus but then did not last year, saying they would only split this way if after the mileage split the class was extremely large.<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fierodave2001||05-25-2001||12:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHarry:<BR><B>Fiero"Dave"2001,<P>My best guess for you would be go for the historical class. I feel either way you go you are a shoe in and this would give others in "stock" a chance at first place.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I've never banked on being a "shoe-in"<P>I've seen many cars that were really close competition in the last few shows.<P>I have a lot of things to work on before the next show. <P>While the judges were looking at my car, they showed me areas that need improvement.<BR>Lots of things I'd never think of were looked at.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||FieroHarry||05-25-2001||08:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierochic88:<BR><B>Are the cars definitely being separated to roof type no matter what?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats the way they have advertised the judging rules in Fiero Owners Magazine and the flyers for the show.<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000019||FieroHarry||05-25-2001||08:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierodave2001:<BR><B>I have a lot of things to work on before the next show. <P>While the judges were looking at my car, they showed me areas that need improvement.<BR>Lots of things I'd never think of were looked at.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Never underestimate judges at cars shows.<BR>Ive seen them pop up headlights to see just how clean they are. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>They love looking for mouse beds in headlight buckets etc etc etc.<P><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
