Z||000022||FieroHarry||05-25-2001||06:46 PM||||Okay here it is copied from my clipboard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>CLASSIFICATIONS: 2001<BR>Classes are the same as in 2000.<BR>CLASS: w/Peer judging<BR>Class A Coupe '84-88<BR>Class B SE 4cyl ‘84-88<BR>Class C SE 6 cyl ‘85-88<BR>Class D Pace Car<BR>Class E GT 1985<BR>Class F GT 1987<BR>Class G GT 1988<BR>Class H Pace Car<BR>Class I Formula<BR>Class J 1986 GT<BR>Section:<BR>1. less than 50K miles<BR>2. between 50-130 K miles<BR>3. between 130-190K miles<BR>4. 190K miles plus<BR>Special:<BR>a. plain roof<BR>b. sunroof<BR>c. T-top<BR>Stage:<BR>1. Stock<BR>2. Restored less than 50%<BR>3. Restored more than 50%<BR>4. Restored 100%<BR>In this group (Stock) you will be allowed at<BR>least 5 small changes. No wheel changes.<BR>Car should still look basically stock. When<BR>you register you will decide your Registration<BR>number from the list above. You will<BR>have to pick 1 group of 2 letters and 2<BR>numbers. For example your registration will<BR>look like this: Stock/Class F/Section<BR>3/Special c/Stage3<BR>To be written like [S/F/3/c/3], which<BR>means that you have a Stock 1987 GT<BR>with 140K miles and a T-top with more<BR>than 50% restoration. (5 selections)<BR>As you can see there arc 9 classes in stock<BR>group. It is imperative that you fill in the<BR>group, class, section, special and stage<BR>numbers and letters when you register.<BR>When the judges are totaling the votes they<BR>will look to see if you have a t-top. sunroof,<BR>or plain roof. You will only be judged<BR>against those cars in your classif ication.<BR>GROUP: Custom judged<BR>Class AA-Coupe<BR>Class BB- GT<BR>If we have too many cars we can separate<BR>these 2 two classes into early and late. (AA1<BR>84-86 E) (AA2 87-88 L) (BB1 E) (BB2 L).<BR>Section<BR>1. Between 10K-100K miles<BR>2. More than 100K: miles<BR>Special:<BR>a. plain roof<BR>b. sunroof<BR>c. T-tops<BR>In the Custom group you are allowed up to<BR>10 changes. This is where you have taken a<BR>basically stock car and personalized it. Paint,<BR>wheels & tires. floormats, side scoops, and<BR>small mechanical upgrades. updates, addon<BR>etc. Display boards optional.<BR>When you register you will have a registration<BR>number that consists of:<BR>5. Group = Custom<BR>6. Class – AA or BB<BR>Section 2<BR>7. Special roof info<BR>So if you have a Coupe 1988 with more<BR>than 150K miles with a T-top Number is<BR>[C/AA/2/C].<BR>GROUP: Semi-Mod judged<BR>In this section is where people have really<BR>been upgrading their Fieros however they<BR>have not done complete systems. Side<BR>scoops, wheels & tires, suspension mods,<BR>anything short of complete engine changes.<BR>Displays are encouraged, listing what you<BR>have done to your car. Judged on present ation,<BR>cleanliness and not personal prefe rence.<BR>Class: Class AAA = Coupe<BR>Class BBB = GT<BR>Class CCC = either in progress<BR>Section:<BR>1. Between 50K-140K miles<BR>2. More than 140K miles<BR>Registration would read like this: SM/AAA-<BR>2 Which would read Semi-Mod Coupe (Yr)<BR>with more than 140K miles. These cars<BR>should have displays. Not mandatory, however<BR>it would make the judges aware of all<BR>your hard work.<BR>Group: Full-Mod judged<BR>Fully Modified group is where the fully<BR>changed engines, upgraded and integrated<BR>packages, body changes, suspension packages,<BR>wheels & tires etc.<BR>Class: 4A = Coupe<BR>4B = GT<BR>4C = unfinished<BR>Section:<BR>1. Wheels & Tires<BR>2. Graphics<BR>3. Just engine changes<BR>4. Engine changes & body. and<BR>interior changes.<BR>5. Display<BR>6. In progress<BR>To fill out the registration form you would<BR>have registration number like this: FM/4B-<BR>1-4-5. List all the numbers that apply from<BR>the section. This would be read Full Mod GT<BR>with wheels tires. Engine and body changes<BR>with display, these things will be the areas<BR>that will be considered during judging. Mileage<BR>doesn't count in this class, However<BR>quality of workmanship. presentation. and<BR>cleanliness do.<BR>GROUP: Replicars<BR>Class Replicars.<BR>R1 = Pro built<BR>R2 = Owner built<BR>Selection:<BR>a. exterior only<BR>b. exterior, interior only<BR>c. exterior, interior and engine<BR>Your registration will look like this R/1/c<BR>Which reads Replicar group. Pro built class<BR>with exterior, interior and engine changes.<BR>These cars should also have displays to<BR>show the judges the information about the<BR>car.<BR>GROUP: Historical<BR>This is just a different name for the 100%<BR>as built collector car. Care have to be as<BR>built. No changes at all, has to be as built.<BR>CLASS: HX1 Coupe<BR>HX2 GT<BR>Section: Mileage (low docs count here)<BR>NOTICE: These changes in the way you<BR>register your car will take a little thinking on<BR>your part. The classes are basically the<BR>same, just a more finite way of making divisional<BR>lines. Not all classes will have the<BR>same groupings, Stock has the most to consider.<BR>Upon registration you will be assigned<BR>the final number which will be the tail end<BR>of the line.<BR>These guidelines (your registration numbers)<BR>will appear on your window card. This<BR>tells the judges just what they are looking<BR>at. We are trying to make the judging more<BR>equitable for all. We want to give away lots<BR>of trophies.<BR>There will be additional trophies for<BR>1. Best graphics<BR>2. Best: show display<BR>3. Best artistic paint<BR>4. Best original stock paint<BR>5. Best new paint stock (GM)<BR>6. Best new paint Non-GM<BR>7. Best prepared car - female<BR>8. Hard luck<BR>9. Longest distance driven<BR>10. Highest mileage<BR>11. Lowest mileage<BR>12. Pontiac Preference Award<BR>13. Silver Sweepstakes Awards<BR>14. Best Engineered<BR>15. Peoples Choice<BR>16. Best of Show<BR>Please take a few minutes to read and reread<BR>these classifications. You are in control<BR>of your own classification. If you have experience<BR>as a car show judge please sign up<BR>as a volunteer. You will be asked to not<BR>judge your own class.<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
